# Thursday film picture economy (locked 2026-08-27)

**Source:** Ben via Video Creator · supersedes the expensive “Omni the whole film” habit (Europa / Neutron minute path).
**Do not invent a second stack.** This file + `00_Brand/Channel-Setup/OMNI_LONGFORM_PLAYBOOK.md` are the canonical pipeline. Older Europa Omni-per-minute lessons remain historical reference only.

Picture-first open · Premiere/Mac assemble · Auditor · remint · affiliate-named-in-film locks stay. Do not weaken them.

## Engine split (hard)

| Job | Tool | Where |
|-----|------|--------|
| Cinematic **WORLD** plates | **Veo** (Fast default; Quality only for one earned hero) | **Google AI Studio** |
| Animate **Orbit** the orange robot | **Omni** — and **only** then | Google AI Studio |
| Stills / composition boards | AI Studio image gen | Google AI Studio |
| Narration | ElevenLabs Ben Orbit Narrator only | Mac |
| Assemble | VO · captions · last card · picture-first open | Mac (as now) |
| Thumbs / pins / Premiere finish | YouTube Studio | Studio |

- **Stay in Google AI Studio.** Do not run the whole Thursday film through Omni.
- **No Kling** unless volume later outgrows Google (Ben lifts this explicitly).
- Mute / strip **Veo baked audio** so it does not fight the VO (`generate_audio=False` + strip on download).

## Film shape

- Runtime **7–9 min** (Last Star / Europa pattern). Expand later only with impressions + hold past ~5 min.
- **Picture-first:** first **3s** = world only. No Orbit, no logo, no title.
- **World does the science.** Orbit appears in **only 1–2 scenes**, and only when the beat is inquisitive or story-narrative (“you're probably wondering…”). Not a tourist sticker on every plate.
- After parts lock: mid-film chapter cards · soft-join · **10s last-picture hold** for Studio end screens → broadcast master. No brand sting. No baked like/subscribe.

## Economy (stills first)

1. In AI Studio, lock stills **before** motion:
   - **One open still** — strange world, **no Orbit**
   - **Two science plates** — planets, ice volcanoes, real detail (aliens only if *this* film is about them)
   - **One Orbit reference still** — canonical identity; use only for the 1–2 Orbit beats
2. Animate only **2–3 money shots** on **Veo Fast** (~8s).
3. Upgrade **one** hero to **Veo Quality** only if it earns the thumb.
4. Use **first-and-last-frame** on the open still so that week’s Shorts loop off the same world.
5. Omni **only** for the Orbit money shots that need the orange robot moving — never for world B-roll.

## Assemble + Shorts

1. Mac assemble as now: Ben Orbit Narrator VO · captions · last card · picture-first open. Mute Veo beds under VO.
2. **4–8** punch Shorts **22–27s** (`orbit-shorts-punch-first`): picture in **1s**, custom picture thumb **no Orbit**, exact listing title on screen, CTA that week’s Thursday film id, **zero `/go/`**.
3. **Long thumbs:** picture + a short SEA-style hook. **No Orbit. No generic CTA.**

## Do not

- Omni the whole Thursday film / ~8–10 Omni plates per VO minute (retired expensive habit)
- Default Kling, ElevenLabs Image & Video, or Seedance for new CG
- Park Orbit in every scene or restore “Orbit after ~8s on every film”
- Weaken picture-first / Auditor / remint / affiliate-named-in-film locks

